A demo whose output is much smaller than its input may encode information from repeated panels separated by full-width rows or columns. Avoid defaulting to an in-place transformation. Segment the input at separators, compare each panel's marker pattern and background against the compact output, and derive the panel-to-output mapping from multiple demos. Account for all output cells and the distractors/unchanged panels. Request a distinguishing demo if panel selection, orientation, or aggregation remains ambiguous; do not submit an unverified aggregate.
